1
00:01:32,750 --> 00:01:35,030
[Forging Justice]

2
00:01:35,200 --> 00:01:37,710
[Episode 16]

3
00:01:39,870 --> 00:01:40,509
What if...

4
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:42,039
I mean what if

5
00:01:42,310 --> 00:01:43,640
a death sentence is actually wrong?

6
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:44,560
What should we do?

7
00:01:44,560 --> 00:01:45,070
Xia,

8
00:01:46,200 --> 00:01:47,400
if you're worried about

9
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,039
taking accountability later on.

10
00:01:49,039 --> 00:01:50,000
I can tell you

11
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:50,759
with full confidence—

12
00:01:50,759 --> 00:01:52,509
we're both on the hook for this one.

13
00:01:52,509 --> 00:01:54,370
Neither of us is getting out of it.

14
00:02:01,150 --> 00:02:01,640
So,

15
00:02:03,310 --> 00:02:05,110
if he does get the death penalty,

16
00:02:06,040 --> 00:02:07,200
are you hoping

17
00:02:10,750 --> 00:02:11,750
that Qian Xingliang stays

18
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:12,810
locked up for good?

19
00:02:31,800 --> 00:02:33,460
Still digging through files?

20
00:02:34,960 --> 00:02:36,360
I'm about to lose my mind.

21
00:02:38,710 --> 00:02:39,800
Still no result

22
00:02:39,840 --> 00:02:40,520
from the Adjudication Committee?

23
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:40,910
No.

24
00:02:41,310 --> 00:02:41,840
I don't know when

25
00:02:41,840 --> 00:02:43,240
the result will come out.

26
00:02:45,910 --> 00:02:47,970
When's your case getting sentenced?

27
00:02:49,280 --> 00:02:49,940
No word yet.

28
00:02:50,079 --> 00:02:50,680
Just wait.

29
00:02:51,710 --> 00:02:52,430
Give me the menu.

30
00:02:52,430 --> 00:02:53,030
Thank you.

31
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:55,280
Why don't you order?

32
00:02:55,280 --> 00:02:55,590
Take a look.

33
00:02:55,590 --> 00:02:56,560
I just ordered a few.

34
00:02:56,560 --> 00:02:57,290
You go ahead.

35
00:02:57,430 --> 00:02:58,030
You order.

36
00:02:58,079 --> 00:02:58,470
Look.

37
00:02:58,910 --> 00:03:00,080
He already ordered, right?

38
00:03:00,080 --> 00:03:01,340
Then serve the dishes.

39
00:03:01,470 --> 00:03:01,800
Okay.

40
00:03:03,870 --> 00:03:04,910
What's the rush?

41
00:03:05,030 --> 00:03:06,430
Let's eat first. No rush.

42
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:07,490
Just spit it out.

43
00:03:09,840 --> 00:03:11,100
Nothing. Just dinner.

44
00:03:11,910 --> 00:03:13,430
By the way,

45
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:16,040
I'm getting married.

46
00:03:16,560 --> 00:03:17,160
That's it.

47
00:03:24,310 --> 00:03:25,510
Who are you marrying?

48
00:03:25,630 --> 00:03:26,630
Fang Leiming,
Deputy Commander of the Military District.

49
00:03:26,630 --> 00:03:27,490
Do you know him?

50
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:28,480
His daughter.

51
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:37,910
Okay.

52
00:03:40,710 --> 00:03:41,240
Got it.

53
00:03:46,120 --> 00:03:46,840
I heard you.

54
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:53,450
Yu, I don't want to
lose my temper with you.

55
00:03:53,470 --> 00:03:54,730
But I'm a little angry.

56
00:03:55,240 --> 00:03:55,910
Not because

57
00:03:55,910 --> 00:03:57,520
you're suddenly getting married,

58
00:03:57,520 --> 00:03:58,560
and not because we used to date.

59
00:03:58,560 --> 00:03:59,680
I got over that long ago.

60
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:00,680
It doesn't matter.

61
00:04:00,680 --> 00:04:02,000
What angers me is your approach

62
00:04:02,000 --> 00:04:03,060
and your attitude.

63
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:07,960
It's always that same

64
00:04:07,960 --> 00:04:09,120
Yu Gaoyuan way.

65
00:04:09,560 --> 00:04:10,590
Looks like you don't care,

66
00:04:10,590 --> 00:04:12,080
but it's all carefully planned

67
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,250
to inform us.

68
00:04:13,630 --> 00:04:15,030
We are all busy.

69
00:04:15,960 --> 00:04:16,920
You make us feel like

70
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,000
we're just some item

71
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:19,120
on your to-do list.

72
00:04:19,140 --> 00:04:20,000
I don't want to be

73
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:21,120
on your to-do list.

74
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:26,130
Congratulations.

75
00:04:27,630 --> 00:04:28,490
Take your time.

76
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,290
I'm leaving.

77
00:04:40,840 --> 00:04:41,900
Why all of a sudden?

78
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:45,070
I'm at that age. Family's been pushing.

79
00:04:48,310 --> 00:04:48,870
How long?

80
00:04:49,510 --> 00:04:50,270
Not long.

81
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:51,940
But she's really nice,

82
00:04:52,430 --> 00:04:53,800
with a great personality.

83
00:04:53,800 --> 00:04:54,800
We get along well.

84
00:04:56,070 --> 00:04:56,870
Oh, and if you get a chance,

85
00:04:56,870 --> 00:04:58,120
tell Yingjie—

86
00:04:58,720 --> 00:05:00,180
she's got a limp in one leg.

87
00:05:00,750 --> 00:05:01,950
If you run into her,

88
00:05:02,360 --> 00:05:03,760
don't act too surprised.

89
00:05:07,750 --> 00:05:08,190
OK.

90
00:05:09,430 --> 00:05:10,760
As long as you're happy.

91
00:05:10,950 --> 00:05:12,010
Congratulations.

92
00:05:15,600 --> 00:05:16,130
Mr. Yuan.

93
00:05:16,360 --> 00:05:17,830
We'll grab dinner once we arrive.

94
00:05:17,830 --> 00:05:19,480
I've got the private room booked.

95
00:05:19,480 --> 00:05:20,270
Mr. Lu asked me

96
00:05:20,270 --> 00:05:21,270
to pay in advance,

97
00:05:21,270 --> 00:05:22,190
so they'll wait for us

98
00:05:22,190 --> 00:05:23,190
no matter how late.

99
00:05:23,190 --> 00:05:24,310
Need accommodations?

100
00:05:24,310 --> 00:05:25,570
Don't worry, Mr. Yuan.

101
00:05:25,870 --> 00:05:27,390
I've arranged everything well.

102
00:05:27,390 --> 00:05:28,390
This trip is about

103
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:30,210
getting both fame and fortune.

104
00:05:37,680 --> 00:05:38,310
Which way?

105
00:05:39,490 --> 00:05:40,040
That way.

106
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:46,440
I've always believed

107
00:05:47,370 --> 00:05:48,120
that all people are equal

108
00:05:48,120 --> 00:05:49,480
before the law.

109
00:05:51,870 --> 00:05:53,870
Just because of some piece of paper,

110
00:05:53,870 --> 00:05:55,040
the one who killed my daughter

111
00:05:55,040 --> 00:05:55,920
gets to walk?

112
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,040
I don't buy it.

113
00:05:59,120 --> 00:06:00,240
If that's how it is,

114
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:02,930
then forgive me.

115
00:06:02,950 --> 00:06:03,680
For the rest of my life,

116
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,010
I'm doing nothing else.

117
00:06:05,830 --> 00:06:07,230
I'll give up everything.

118
00:06:07,430 --> 00:06:09,120
I'll fight him to the end.

119
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:22,120
My daughter

120
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:23,860
jumped into the river.

121
00:06:25,800 --> 00:06:27,660
They searched for two whole days.

122
00:06:29,160 --> 00:06:31,020
I went down to look for her before.

123
00:06:31,870 --> 00:06:32,800
The water

124
00:06:35,310 --> 00:06:36,370
was freezing cold.

125
00:06:42,040 --> 00:06:42,800
My daughter

126
00:06:43,510 --> 00:06:45,800
was soaking in that water for two days.

127
00:07:01,950 --> 00:07:02,480
Mr. Qiao.

128
00:07:04,000 --> 00:07:04,930
As things stand,

129
00:07:06,070 --> 00:07:07,600
it's very difficult

130
00:07:07,870 --> 00:07:08,800
to legally prove

131
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:11,190
that your daughter's suicide

132
00:07:11,190 --> 00:07:12,480
was directly caused

133
00:07:13,600 --> 00:07:14,390
by Song Xiaoguang.

134
00:07:14,390 --> 00:07:16,390
That's what all those bastards say.

135
00:07:16,720 --> 00:07:18,430
You shouldn't say that too.

136
00:07:19,180 --> 00:07:20,770
Please watch your tone.

137
00:07:21,750 --> 00:07:22,280
Mr. Qiao.

138
00:07:22,750 --> 00:07:23,680
Mr. Yuan

139
00:07:23,870 --> 00:07:25,070
really wants to help you.

140
00:07:25,070 --> 00:07:26,040
But we're lawyers.

141
00:07:26,040 --> 00:07:27,310
We have to assess the situation

142
00:07:27,310 --> 00:07:28,240
from a legal standpoint

143
00:07:28,240 --> 00:07:30,100
to find a way to actually help you.

144
00:07:31,430 --> 00:07:32,690
Up to this point,

145
00:07:33,310 --> 00:07:34,390
I haven't obtained

146
00:07:35,510 --> 00:07:37,000
authorization from any party

147
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:38,260
involved in this case,

148
00:07:39,360 --> 00:07:40,220
including you.

149
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:42,240
So,

150
00:07:43,159 --> 00:07:44,620
there's not much I can say.

151
00:07:51,560 --> 00:07:52,190
Not much?

152
00:07:56,870 --> 00:07:57,430
I see.

153
00:07:58,950 --> 00:08:00,270
You are here to make money,

154
00:08:00,270 --> 00:08:00,670
right?

155
00:08:01,240 --> 00:08:02,240
I won't make it hard for you.

156
00:08:02,240 --> 00:08:04,190
If I wanted money, I wouldn't be here.

157
00:08:04,190 --> 00:08:05,250
I can do it for free.

158
00:08:08,360 --> 00:08:09,870
Mr. Qiao, calm down.

159
00:08:10,070 --> 00:08:11,680
Let Mr. Yuan finish.

160
00:08:11,830 --> 00:08:13,040
Alright, I'll finish.

161
00:08:13,040 --> 00:08:14,720
My initial plan was

162
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,210
to start with the accomplices.

163
00:08:17,350 --> 00:08:18,760
By defending them,

164
00:08:19,070 --> 00:08:20,680
we could expose Song Xiaoguang.

165
00:08:20,680 --> 00:08:21,920
Defend them?

166
00:08:23,510 --> 00:08:25,110
Do they even need defending?

167
00:08:26,260 --> 00:08:27,600
They're all vicious thugs

168
00:08:27,600 --> 00:08:28,630
and murderers!

169
00:08:28,680 --> 00:08:30,690
What they need is a bullet!

170
00:08:31,070 --> 00:08:31,560
What?

171
00:08:31,950 --> 00:08:33,350
They're paying you more?

172
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:35,120
I already told you

173
00:08:35,510 --> 00:08:36,620
I'm not coming for money.

174
00:08:36,620 --> 00:08:38,679
-I really can do it for free.
-Well...

175
00:08:40,789 --> 00:08:41,390
Mr. Qiao,

176
00:08:41,789 --> 00:08:43,240
we came all the way here.

177
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:44,159
How about

178
00:08:44,790 --> 00:08:45,930
you go back and think about it?

179
00:08:45,930 --> 00:08:47,590
Let's talk when you calm down.

180
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:53,780
You're all birds of a feather.

181
00:08:54,210 --> 00:08:55,360
I can do it for free!

182
00:09:00,790 --> 00:09:01,320
Mr. Qiao.

183
00:09:02,440 --> 00:09:02,770
Here.

184
00:09:03,030 --> 00:09:04,760
Please sit down and hear me out.

185
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:06,120
I can do it for free.

186
00:09:06,120 --> 00:09:06,390
Sit.

187
00:09:08,030 --> 00:09:09,480
We can start

188
00:09:10,120 --> 00:09:11,600
by filing a civil claim

189
00:09:12,120 --> 00:09:14,320
attached to the criminal prosecution.

190
00:09:14,360 --> 00:09:15,840
You're the victim's family.

191
00:09:15,840 --> 00:09:17,360
I'll serve as your legal representative

192
00:09:17,360 --> 00:09:18,870
and seek compensation from the defendant.

193
00:09:18,870 --> 00:09:20,400
I don't need compensation.

194
00:09:20,670 --> 00:09:21,610
I don't need money.

195
00:09:21,610 --> 00:09:24,010
Even if you don't,
I can still do it for free.

196
00:09:24,240 --> 00:09:25,900
Can money bring my daughter back?

197
00:09:25,900 --> 00:09:26,750
What I want is

198
00:09:26,750 --> 00:09:28,200
to drag Song Xiaoguang out

199
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:29,360
and bring him to justice!

200
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:29,750
Yes!

201
00:09:29,870 --> 00:09:31,670
Drag Song Xiaoguang out, right?

202
00:09:31,870 --> 00:09:32,800
Leave that to us!

203
00:09:35,030 --> 00:09:37,430
We'll drag him out
and see him face justice!

204
00:09:38,270 --> 00:09:39,400
But the condition is

205
00:09:40,030 --> 00:09:40,870
that you believe in us,

206
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:41,440
trust us,

207
00:09:42,360 --> 00:09:43,290
and listen to me—

208
00:09:43,840 --> 00:09:44,570
is that okay?

209
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:51,510
Mr. Qiao.

210
00:09:51,510 --> 00:09:53,310
You're the boss at your company.

211
00:09:53,390 --> 00:09:54,630
You call the shots, right?

212
00:09:54,630 --> 00:09:56,150
At this firm, I'm also the boss.

213
00:09:56,150 --> 00:09:57,080
I call the shots.

214
00:10:10,750 --> 00:10:12,150
Come on, let's do a toast.

215
00:10:26,030 --> 00:10:27,360
The phone number from Bieshan Prison.

216
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,090
Call Zhang Lihui to cheer her up

217
00:10:29,400 --> 00:10:30,480
when you have time.

218
00:10:32,630 --> 00:10:34,030
You'd better not.

219
00:10:34,390 --> 00:10:36,320
You're married now.

220
00:10:36,350 --> 00:10:37,350
Not appropriate.

221
00:10:39,390 --> 00:10:40,520
When's the wedding?

222
00:10:40,790 --> 00:10:43,190
No wedding, nobody's going to come anyway.

223
00:10:43,360 --> 00:10:44,120
There you go again.

224
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:45,390
Getting all sensitive again.

225
00:10:45,390 --> 00:10:47,250
Paranoia, persecution complex.

226
00:10:47,750 --> 00:10:48,440
You're not even

227
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,360
gonna invite us?

228
00:10:49,360 --> 00:10:51,480
You're invited, just a simple dinner.

229
00:10:51,480 --> 00:10:53,030
Anyway, when I get married,

230
00:10:53,030 --> 00:10:54,360
you all better be there.

231
00:10:54,360 --> 00:10:56,080
I don't care about the well-wishes,

232
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:57,840
but the gift money better be solid.

233
00:10:57,840 --> 00:10:58,200
OK.

234
00:10:58,750 --> 00:10:59,950
Who are you marrying?

235
00:10:59,960 --> 00:11:00,720
Who?

236
00:11:01,360 --> 00:11:02,000
Ding Rui.

237
00:11:02,270 --> 00:11:03,130
Who's Ding Rui?

238
00:11:03,270 --> 00:11:04,470
Didn't I mention her?

239
00:11:04,720 --> 00:11:05,720
Ding Zhongxiang.

240
00:11:06,150 --> 00:11:08,010
The daughter of Court Pres. Ding.

241
00:11:08,320 --> 00:11:09,150
Since when?

242
00:11:10,920 --> 00:11:12,630
Even though I'm based in Beijing,

243
00:11:12,630 --> 00:11:13,600
my heart

244
00:11:13,960 --> 00:11:14,960
is still in Nanyu.

245
00:11:15,240 --> 00:11:16,030
Deep down,

246
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:17,270
I've always seen myself

247
00:11:17,270 --> 00:11:18,200
half a son

248
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:18,790
of Nanyu.

249
00:11:20,910 --> 00:11:21,710
You really...

250
00:11:21,940 --> 00:11:23,140
You never miss a beat.

251
00:11:24,550 --> 00:11:26,110
Did you contact the victim's family?

252
00:11:26,110 --> 00:11:27,130
We've signed the representation agreement.

253
00:11:27,130 --> 00:11:27,860
It went well.

254
00:11:28,510 --> 00:11:30,170
Except the money was a bit low.

255
00:11:30,240 --> 00:11:31,080
For the fame.

256
00:11:31,280 --> 00:11:32,150
Why's the money an issue?

257
00:11:32,150 --> 00:11:32,880
He's loaded.

258
00:11:34,390 --> 00:11:35,870
He's stubborn as a mule.

259
00:11:35,870 --> 00:11:37,750
Took me forever
just to get through to him.

260
00:11:37,750 --> 00:11:38,670
If he weren't so stubborn,

261
00:11:38,670 --> 00:11:40,320
we wouldn't be able to pull this off.

262
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,120
Several of the victims

263
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:42,050
were about to give up.

264
00:11:42,050 --> 00:11:43,250
I talked them back in.

265
00:11:45,390 --> 00:11:45,960
Did he

266
00:11:45,960 --> 00:11:47,220
refer this case to you?

267
00:11:52,080 --> 00:11:52,740
Yu Gaoyuan.

268
00:11:52,790 --> 00:11:54,270
You're a judge.

269
00:11:54,730 --> 00:11:56,600
Is it appropriate for you to refer lawyers

270
00:11:56,600 --> 00:11:57,390
to victims?

271
00:12:00,590 --> 00:12:02,050
Whether they take the case

272
00:12:02,150 --> 00:12:03,650
depends on their willingness, doesn't it?

273
00:12:03,650 --> 00:12:05,390
And they just happened to be willing.

274
00:12:05,390 --> 00:12:06,550
But it's also not appropriate for him

275
00:12:06,550 --> 00:12:08,210
to refer business to a lawyer.

276
00:12:08,670 --> 00:12:10,270
You work in the court system.

277
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,820
If you don't follow the law

278
00:12:11,960 --> 00:12:13,080
and don't follow procedure,

279
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,420
how can you let others obey it?

280
00:12:14,420 --> 00:12:15,780
So what, we just sit here

281
00:12:16,030 --> 00:12:16,560
and chat,

282
00:12:16,790 --> 00:12:17,400
debate philosophy,

283
00:12:17,400 --> 00:12:18,360
and wait for Song Xiaoguang

284
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:20,730
to walk out of the mental hospital
on his own?

285
00:12:20,730 --> 00:12:21,910
Or should I just go straight
to the Court Pres.

286
00:12:21,910 --> 00:12:22,370
and say,

287
00:12:22,440 --> 00:12:23,240
"Court Pres.,

288
00:12:23,240 --> 00:12:25,000
you've gotta be willing to risk it all—

289
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:26,390
Song Xiaoguang, Secretary Song—

290
00:12:26,390 --> 00:12:27,550
they gotta be taken down.

291
00:12:27,550 --> 00:12:28,670
Forget about the career."

292
00:12:28,670 --> 00:12:29,730
Don't give me that.

293
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,670
We all learned

294
00:12:30,870 --> 00:12:31,720
that substantive justice

295
00:12:31,720 --> 00:12:32,720
only has meaning

296
00:12:32,720 --> 00:12:33,910
when it's achieved

297
00:12:34,030 --> 00:12:34,770
through procedural justice.

298
00:12:34,770 --> 00:12:36,320
So what's the point of doing that?

299
00:12:36,320 --> 00:12:36,720
Fine.

300
00:12:38,120 --> 00:12:39,180
Let me ask you this:

301
00:12:39,250 --> 00:12:40,120
If justice comes late,

302
00:12:40,120 --> 00:12:41,270
is it still justice?

303
00:12:42,550 --> 00:12:43,480
Wait five years,

304
00:12:43,550 --> 00:12:44,720
ten, fifty years—

305
00:12:45,200 --> 00:12:45,960
Song Xiaoguang

306
00:12:45,960 --> 00:12:46,690
surrounded by his kids and grandkids,

307
00:12:46,690 --> 00:12:47,810
dies of old age,

308
00:12:47,840 --> 00:12:48,720
and the day before he dies, someone says,

309
00:12:48,720 --> 00:12:49,630
"You're guilty. You're under arrest."

310
00:12:49,630 --> 00:12:50,510
Can you accept it?

311
00:12:50,510 --> 00:12:51,410
Well, let me ask you:

312
00:12:51,410 --> 00:12:52,080
If justice is late,

313
00:12:52,080 --> 00:12:53,610
why isn't it still justice?

314
00:12:54,120 --> 00:12:55,910
Isn't it better than no justice at all?

315
00:12:55,910 --> 00:12:56,460
You can say

316
00:12:56,460 --> 00:12:57,600
that justice is flawed,

317
00:12:57,600 --> 00:12:58,570
but you can't deny

318
00:12:58,570 --> 00:12:59,440
that it's still justice.

319
00:12:59,440 --> 00:13:00,020
Don't give me

320
00:13:00,020 --> 00:13:01,510
all this philosophical crap.

321
00:13:01,510 --> 00:13:02,320
In this case,

322
00:13:02,530 --> 00:13:04,200
putting Song Xiaoguang
in the defendant's seat

323
00:13:04,200 --> 00:13:06,460
is the simplest and most direct justice.

324
00:13:06,550 --> 00:13:07,030
If we can't even do that,

325
00:13:07,030 --> 00:13:08,760
forget about everything else.

326
00:13:09,510 --> 00:13:09,910
Let me ask you—

327
00:13:09,910 --> 00:13:11,570
did I take a kickback from you?

328
00:13:11,720 --> 00:13:12,390
If you did,

329
00:13:12,470 --> 00:13:13,730
you shouldn't be here.

330
00:13:13,860 --> 00:13:14,840
Alright, why is it

331
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,840
that every meal turns into a debate?

332
00:13:18,760 --> 00:13:19,910
We rarely get together.

333
00:13:19,910 --> 00:13:21,030
Can we not fight?

334
00:13:28,550 --> 00:13:29,990
Does Mr. Yuan know you two are doing this?

335
00:13:29,990 --> 00:13:30,850
No, he doesn't.

336
00:13:31,150 --> 00:13:31,910
He was so busy.

337
00:13:31,910 --> 00:13:33,120
He didn't even wanna take it at first.

338
00:13:33,120 --> 00:13:33,720
Chen Yizhong, listen to me,

339
00:13:33,720 --> 00:13:35,380
you've got double standards.

340
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,210
How do I have double standards?

341
00:13:38,000 --> 00:13:39,860
They're both hooliganism charges.

342
00:13:39,860 --> 00:13:40,720
In the Wang Youxi case,

343
00:13:40,720 --> 00:13:41,650
you thought the max sentence
wasn't enough,

344
00:13:41,650 --> 00:13:42,910
so you pushed for more.

345
00:13:43,200 --> 00:13:44,840
But with Song Xiaoguang, what happens?

346
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:45,930
You've changed your tune.

347
00:13:45,930 --> 00:13:47,130
Ordinary people are easy to bully,

348
00:13:47,130 --> 00:13:48,250
so you press them hard.

349
00:13:48,250 --> 00:13:49,240
But for the official's kid
with connections,

350
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,510
suddenly it's all about
procedural justice?

351
00:13:50,510 --> 00:13:51,240
Come on, explain yourself.

352
00:13:51,240 --> 00:13:52,500
What tune did I change?

353
00:13:52,790 --> 00:13:53,990
Go ask Xia Yingjie.

354
00:13:54,600 --> 00:13:55,320
In the Qian Xingliang case,

355
00:13:55,320 --> 00:13:56,480
she also went to Mr. Yuan.

356
00:13:56,480 --> 00:13:57,320
But she was

357
00:13:57,630 --> 00:13:58,430
saving a life.

358
00:13:59,080 --> 00:13:59,540
And you?

359
00:13:59,870 --> 00:14:01,480
You're trying to destroy someone.

360
00:14:01,480 --> 00:14:03,210
I'm trying to destroy someone?

361
00:14:04,480 --> 00:14:05,480
I'm a prosecutor.

362
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:07,280
I fight criminal activity.

363
00:14:07,440 --> 00:14:08,240
What's wrong?

364
00:14:08,570 --> 00:14:09,540
That's my duty.

365
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,600
What, did I hit a nerve?

366
00:14:10,600 --> 00:14:11,840
Getting so defensive?

367
00:14:11,840 --> 00:14:12,360
If you think

368
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:13,480
there's a problem with our materials,

369
00:14:13,480 --> 00:14:14,510
then return the file.

370
00:14:14,510 --> 00:14:15,630
If you think my opinion

371
00:14:15,630 --> 00:14:16,150
has issues,

372
00:14:16,150 --> 00:14:17,120
you don't have to adopt it.

373
00:14:17,120 --> 00:14:18,030
Don't talk to me like that.

374
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:18,790
No fighting.

375
00:14:19,080 --> 00:14:20,320
Once the verdict comes out
in a couple days,

376
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:20,980
you'll see.

377
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:21,530
Alright?

378
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:26,720
Wasn't our last dinner

379
00:14:26,720 --> 00:14:27,720
in this same room?

380
00:14:28,270 --> 00:14:29,870
This room seems to be jinxed.

381
00:14:30,030 --> 00:14:30,960
From now on,

382
00:14:30,960 --> 00:14:32,560
we're not coming here again.

383
00:14:37,510 --> 00:14:38,480
You know, from our class,

384
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:40,150
only you three came to Binjiang.

385
00:14:40,150 --> 00:14:42,510
So how on earth do you get along so well?

386
00:14:44,810 --> 00:14:45,450
By the way,

387
00:14:45,480 --> 00:14:46,510
Mr. Yuan might not take

388
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:47,640
Xia Yingjie's case.

389
00:14:48,600 --> 00:14:49,750
I think that Qian Xingliang

390
00:14:49,750 --> 00:14:50,750
is as good as dead.

391
00:14:53,960 --> 00:14:55,820
Where can I buy Liberation Shoes?

392
00:14:57,550 --> 00:14:58,410
He knows where.

393
00:15:00,440 --> 00:15:02,300
Where can I get Liberation Shoes?

394
00:15:14,080 --> 00:15:14,810
You're back.

395
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:18,750
Finished dinner?

396
00:15:19,200 --> 00:15:19,860
How'd it go?

397
00:15:22,150 --> 00:15:23,320
This is

398
00:15:24,600 --> 00:15:25,030
Zhang Lihui's

399
00:15:25,030 --> 00:15:26,630
number from Bieshan Prison.

400
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:29,480
Lu already gave it to me.

401
00:15:29,480 --> 00:15:30,140
You keep it.

402
00:15:30,870 --> 00:15:31,800
Have you two met?

403
00:15:33,720 --> 00:15:35,850
You came all the way here just for this?

404
00:15:36,480 --> 00:15:36,870
No.

405
00:15:38,240 --> 00:15:39,320
There's something I want you

406
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,720
to answer me honestly.

407
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:44,320
Am I a person

408
00:15:44,320 --> 00:15:45,650
with double standards?

409
00:15:47,120 --> 00:15:47,920
What's wrong?

410
00:15:50,000 --> 00:15:51,000
In the Song Xiaoguang

411
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,200
and Wang Youxi cases—

412
00:15:52,840 --> 00:15:54,120
did my attitude differ

413
00:15:54,120 --> 00:15:55,080
because of

414
00:15:55,080 --> 00:15:56,280
their social status?

415
00:15:57,990 --> 00:15:58,960
These two cases are different.

416
00:15:58,960 --> 00:16:00,080
You can't compare them.

417
00:16:00,080 --> 00:16:00,840
Besides,

418
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:03,840
people inevitably have double standards.

419
00:16:03,840 --> 00:16:05,640
And they aren't even aware of it.

420
00:16:05,750 --> 00:16:06,960
The difference is

421
00:16:07,030 --> 00:16:07,890
to what degree,

422
00:16:08,390 --> 00:16:09,080
and whether you throw a fit

423
00:16:09,080 --> 00:16:10,880
when someone calls you out on it.

424
00:16:12,790 --> 00:16:14,080
I didn't throw a fit, did I?

425
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,000
No.

426
00:16:15,960 --> 00:16:17,820
You're one of the few people I know

427
00:16:17,960 --> 00:16:19,890
who can be honest with themselves.

428
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:23,720
Thank you.

429
00:16:29,780 --> 00:16:30,380
Actually,

430
00:16:30,750 --> 00:16:32,870
whenever I'm full of self-doubt

431
00:16:32,890 --> 00:16:34,060
and feeling down,

432
00:16:36,790 --> 00:16:37,620
you always manage to say something

433
00:16:37,620 --> 00:16:38,680
that pulls me back.

434
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:41,390
I don't have that much power.

435
00:16:42,080 --> 00:16:42,600
Besides,

436
00:16:42,600 --> 00:16:44,400
you have so many mental mentors.

437
00:16:44,880 --> 00:16:46,760
Your father, Mr. Zhou,

438
00:16:46,790 --> 00:16:47,520
aren't they?

439
00:16:48,510 --> 00:16:49,570
That's different.

440
00:16:49,870 --> 00:16:50,960
They educate me.

441
00:16:51,670 --> 00:16:53,270
You actually understand me.

442
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:54,530
That matters.

443
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,240
Actually,

444
00:16:57,910 --> 00:16:58,840
all these years,

445
00:16:59,510 --> 00:17:00,120
you're the only one

446
00:17:00,120 --> 00:17:01,850
I never put my guard up against.

447
00:17:03,120 --> 00:17:03,670
I know.

448
00:17:09,270 --> 00:17:10,730
How about we give it a shot?

449
00:17:11,720 --> 00:17:12,680
Stop.

450
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:15,010
Let's get down to business.

451
00:17:16,349 --> 00:17:16,960
You came to see me,

452
00:17:16,960 --> 00:17:18,349
surely not just to say that,

453
00:17:18,349 --> 00:17:18,750
right?

454
00:17:23,640 --> 00:17:24,000
Yes.

455
00:17:27,270 --> 00:17:29,110
You asked Lu and Mr. Yuan

456
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:30,960
to defend Qian Xingliang?

457
00:17:34,480 --> 00:17:34,880
Yes.

458
00:17:36,110 --> 00:17:37,110
But

459
00:17:37,510 --> 00:17:39,040
Lu thought it was too tough.

460
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,640
He didn't want to waste his time.

461
00:17:40,640 --> 00:17:41,240
He said no.

462
00:17:42,200 --> 00:17:42,920
About this...

463
00:17:42,920 --> 00:17:44,520
I know what you're gonna say.

464
00:17:45,070 --> 00:17:46,310
But I probably won't be

465
00:17:46,310 --> 00:17:48,270
the presiding judge on this case anymore.

466
00:17:48,270 --> 00:17:49,440
So I figured I could

467
00:17:49,440 --> 00:17:51,300
refer a lawyer to Qian Xingliang.

468
00:17:52,240 --> 00:17:53,190
On this one,

469
00:17:53,680 --> 00:17:54,810
I'm with Yu Gaoyuan.

470
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:07,970
Okay.

471
00:18:08,400 --> 00:18:08,750
Here.

472
00:18:32,470 --> 00:18:33,000
Mr. Yuan.

473
00:18:33,310 --> 00:18:35,760
About the Song Xiaoguang case,

474
00:18:35,830 --> 00:18:37,160
we need to fully

475
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:38,350
leverage public opinion.

476
00:18:38,350 --> 00:18:39,400
In the past, I used to say

477
00:18:39,400 --> 00:18:41,290
it's best not to use public opinion.

478
00:18:41,290 --> 00:18:42,820
But this case is different.

479
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:43,430
I see.

480
00:18:43,680 --> 00:18:45,370
I didn't come to talk about that.

481
00:18:45,370 --> 00:18:46,890
About that Mr. Qiao case,

482
00:18:46,920 --> 00:18:47,830
I worked so hard

483
00:18:47,830 --> 00:18:49,070
to negotiate my way up

484
00:18:49,070 --> 00:18:50,000
from a free service to 30,000 yuan.

485
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:50,680
How come, when it gets to you,

486
00:18:50,680 --> 00:18:52,140
it was down to 20,000 yuan?

487
00:18:54,110 --> 00:18:54,480
Well,

488
00:18:55,440 --> 00:18:56,920
that was Ma who negotiated it.

489
00:18:56,920 --> 00:18:57,780
Don't blame Ma.

490
00:18:57,790 --> 00:18:58,680
What's he got to do with it?

491
00:18:58,680 --> 00:18:59,310
I've asked him.

492
00:18:59,310 --> 00:19:00,940
He said you negotiated for 20,000 yuan.

493
00:19:00,940 --> 00:19:02,480
From first instance to appeal—

494
00:19:02,480 --> 00:19:03,240
20,000 yuan?

495
00:19:04,160 --> 00:19:05,640
Excluding travel expenses.

496
00:19:05,640 --> 00:19:06,100
This...

497
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:07,960
What? What travel expenses?

498
00:19:07,960 --> 00:19:09,160
Don't jerk me around.

499
00:19:09,440 --> 00:19:10,400
We've got a whole crew,

500
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,830
travel, food, lodging—

501
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:13,510
we're counting on that 30,000 yuan.

502
00:19:13,510 --> 00:19:14,750
You either charged 500 yuan

503
00:19:14,750 --> 00:19:15,640
or 1,000 yuan for your other cases,

504
00:19:15,640 --> 00:19:16,720
and some you even did for free.

505
00:19:16,720 --> 00:19:18,000
We were counting on squeezing some money

506
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:18,750
out of this Mr. Qiao.

507
00:19:18,750 --> 00:19:20,160
And you're giving him a discount?

508
00:19:20,160 --> 00:19:21,680
He already offered 20,000 yuan.

509
00:19:21,680 --> 00:19:24,010
And you're still talking about expenses?

510
00:19:24,030 --> 00:19:25,120
Zeming,

511
00:19:25,720 --> 00:19:27,790
you should handle
these negotiations later.

512
00:19:27,790 --> 00:19:29,720
I don't have the talent for this.

513
00:19:30,360 --> 00:19:31,960
And Ma's no good at it either.

514
00:19:32,350 --> 00:19:33,070
What does Ma

515
00:19:33,070 --> 00:19:34,270
have to do with it?

516
00:19:35,440 --> 00:19:35,960
Mr. Great Yuan,

517
00:19:35,960 --> 00:19:37,160
I have one question.

518
00:19:37,590 --> 00:19:38,460
If you keep doing business this way,

519
00:19:38,460 --> 00:19:39,550
how's this firm gonna survive?

520
00:19:39,550 --> 00:19:41,150
I make money. You lose money.

521
00:19:41,200 --> 00:19:42,200
That's a problem.

522
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:43,290
Fine.

523
00:19:43,720 --> 00:19:44,370
Since you asked,

524
00:19:44,370 --> 00:19:45,210
I will talk

525
00:19:45,830 --> 00:19:47,400
to you about it.

526
00:19:48,680 --> 00:19:49,740
I have my standards

527
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:52,110
for taking cases.

528
00:19:52,680 --> 00:19:54,080
You have to respect this.

529
00:19:54,270 --> 00:19:55,250
Some cases,

530
00:19:55,330 --> 00:19:56,130
in my opinion,

531
00:19:56,310 --> 00:19:58,510
I won't take no matter how much they pay.

532
00:19:58,870 --> 00:19:59,720
Some cases,

533
00:20:00,310 --> 00:20:02,480
I'll take even if I don't get a dime.

534
00:20:04,310 --> 00:20:05,750
Because I believe that as lawyers,

535
00:20:05,750 --> 00:20:07,550
we ought to uphold our own ideals

536
00:20:08,310 --> 00:20:09,510
and moral standards.

537
00:20:11,270 --> 00:20:11,930
That's all.

538
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:18,960
Noted.

539
00:20:20,040 --> 00:20:20,630
Mentor,

540
00:20:23,910 --> 00:20:25,620
I've got a case here

541
00:20:26,600 --> 00:20:28,510
that fits your value system perfectly.

542
00:20:28,510 --> 00:20:29,440
Not a penny in it.

543
00:20:29,590 --> 00:20:31,790
It's practically tailor-made for you.

544
00:20:32,030 --> 00:20:32,830
Can I share it?

545
00:20:35,310 --> 00:20:35,830
Zeming.

546
00:20:36,760 --> 00:20:37,820
I'm a little tired.

547
00:20:38,440 --> 00:20:39,550
This Song Xiaoguang case

548
00:20:39,550 --> 00:20:40,610
has been draining.

549
00:20:41,120 --> 00:20:42,450
I need to get some sleep.

550
00:20:43,130 --> 00:20:44,200
Just rest here. I'll just talk.

551
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:44,690
No.

552
00:20:44,720 --> 00:20:45,680
-You...
-Just hear me out.

553
00:20:45,680 --> 00:20:46,310
I'm really tired.

554
00:20:46,310 --> 00:20:47,270
About that case,

555
00:20:47,270 --> 00:20:49,160
first instance hasn't come down yet.

556
00:20:49,160 --> 00:20:50,110
It might be a death sentence.

557
00:20:50,110 --> 00:20:51,970
We'd be doing the appeal defense.

558
00:20:52,160 --> 00:20:53,030
And in all these years,

559
00:20:53,030 --> 00:20:54,510
I've never seen

560
00:20:54,510 --> 00:20:55,270
a death penalty conviction

561
00:20:55,270 --> 00:20:56,530
overturned on appeal.

562
00:20:56,840 --> 00:20:58,070
Death penalty to acquittal.

563
00:20:58,070 --> 00:20:59,070
Exciting, right?

564
00:21:02,860 --> 00:21:03,790
Not handling it?

565
00:21:05,010 --> 00:21:05,480
Doesn't this

566
00:21:05,480 --> 00:21:06,920
align with your values?

567
00:21:08,270 --> 00:21:08,800
Fine.

568
00:21:08,830 --> 00:21:10,480
Too bad for him, I guess.

569
00:21:10,500 --> 00:21:11,430
Have a good rest.

570
00:21:25,680 --> 00:21:26,640
When did this case

571
00:21:26,640 --> 00:21:27,590
even come up?

572
00:21:28,890 --> 00:21:30,110
We agreed before coming,

573
00:21:30,110 --> 00:21:30,910
just one case.

574
00:21:36,070 --> 00:21:36,550
Sleep.

575
00:21:37,030 --> 00:21:38,240
I'm not the Monkey King.

576
00:21:38,240 --> 00:21:40,440
I can't alter the Book of Life and Death.

577
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:44,750
In the Wang Youxi case,

578
00:21:44,750 --> 00:21:45,750
you thought the max sentence
wasn't enough,

579
00:21:45,750 --> 00:21:46,750
so you pushed for more.

580
00:21:46,750 --> 00:21:47,830
Go ask Xia Yingjie.

581
00:21:47,920 --> 00:21:48,790
In the Qian Xingliang case,

582
00:21:48,790 --> 00:21:50,000
she also went to Mr. Yuan.

583
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:50,750
But she was

584
00:21:51,110 --> 00:21:51,920
saving a life.

585
00:21:52,510 --> 00:21:53,070
And you?

586
00:21:53,400 --> 00:21:55,330
You're trying to destroy someone.

587
00:21:55,350 --> 00:21:57,010
I don't want blood on my hands.

588
00:21:57,680 --> 00:21:59,610
We're both on the hook for this one.

589
00:21:59,640 --> 00:22:00,880
Because the death penalty

590
00:22:00,880 --> 00:22:02,510
isn't pronounced
by the Adjudication Committee.

591
00:22:02,510 --> 00:22:03,160
It's us.

592
00:22:03,510 --> 00:22:04,350
You and I

593
00:22:04,440 --> 00:22:06,100
hand down the death sentence.

594
00:22:08,400 --> 00:22:08,920
Xia.

595
00:22:11,270 --> 00:22:12,270
I'm a prosecutor.

596
00:22:12,550 --> 00:22:13,960
I fight criminal activity.

597
00:22:13,960 --> 00:22:14,880
That's my duty.

598
00:22:15,310 --> 00:22:15,680
Chen.

599
00:22:16,920 --> 00:22:17,310
Chen.

600
00:22:19,200 --> 00:22:19,730
Let's go.

601
00:22:28,920 --> 00:22:31,850
By decision of the Judicial Committee
of this court,

602
00:22:32,430 --> 00:22:33,960
the judgment is as follows:

603
00:22:35,720 --> 00:22:37,250
The defendant, Wang Youxi,

604
00:22:38,440 --> 00:22:39,970
convicted of hooliganism,

605
00:22:40,440 --> 00:22:41,700
is sentenced to death,

606
00:22:42,310 --> 00:22:45,110
with permanent deprivation
of political rights.

607
00:22:49,790 --> 00:22:51,590
The defendant, Liang Yuemin,

608
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,170
convicted of hooliganism,

609
00:22:54,400 --> 00:22:55,600
is sentenced to death

610
00:22:56,110 --> 00:22:57,720
with a two-year reprieve,

611
00:22:58,190 --> 00:22:58,650
No!

612
00:22:58,680 --> 00:23:00,650
and permanent deprivation
of political rights.

613
00:23:00,650 --> 00:23:01,370
No! No!

614
00:23:02,270 --> 00:23:02,720
No!

615
00:23:03,310 --> 00:23:04,040
We can't die!

616
00:23:04,200 --> 00:23:04,930
We can't die!

617
00:23:04,980 --> 00:23:07,540
W-We were wrong!

618
00:23:08,030 --> 00:23:08,830
We were wrong!

619
00:23:09,000 --> 00:23:10,050
We were wrong! We were wrong!

620
00:23:10,050 --> 00:23:11,010
Wrong! Wrong!

621
00:23:11,160 --> 00:23:12,790
We were wrong! We were wrong!

622
00:23:13,070 --> 00:23:14,220
We confess! We confess!

623
00:23:14,220 --> 00:23:15,790
We're—we're hooligans!

624
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:17,070
W-We are hooligans!

625
00:23:17,070 --> 00:23:18,000
We plead guilty!

626
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:19,400
Your Honor! We can't die!

627
00:23:19,550 --> 00:23:21,510
We have elderly parents at home!

628
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:23,310
My son's only seven!

629
00:23:23,380 --> 00:23:24,140
I can't die.

630
00:23:25,030 --> 00:23:26,240
Well... Your Honor!

631
00:23:26,480 --> 00:23:27,340
How about this?

632
00:23:27,830 --> 00:23:28,680
I'll die!

633
00:23:29,830 --> 00:23:30,640
I'll die!

634
00:23:31,070 --> 00:23:31,800
Let him live.

635
00:23:32,680 --> 00:23:33,270
I'll die!

636
00:23:33,830 --> 00:23:35,790
Just me! Just me!

637
00:23:36,550 --> 00:23:37,670
Let one of us live!

638
00:23:38,310 --> 00:23:39,350
We have a kid!

639
00:23:40,680 --> 00:23:41,480
A kid.

640
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:14,400
In accordance with Articles 43

641
00:24:14,510 --> 00:24:15,680
and 53 of the Criminal Law

642
00:24:15,680 --> 00:24:17,000
of the People's Republic of China,

643
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:18,440
and the Decision of the Standing Committee

644
00:24:18,440 --> 00:24:19,720
of the National People's Congress

645
00:24:19,720 --> 00:24:22,830
on the Severe Punishment of Criminals

646
00:24:22,830 --> 00:24:24,000
Who Seriously Endanger Social Order,

647
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,720
pursuant to Article 1 thereof,

648
00:24:25,720 --> 00:24:27,250
the judgment is as follows:

649
00:24:28,350 --> 00:24:30,310
The defendant, Qian Xingliang,
is sentenced

650
00:24:30,310 --> 00:24:31,110
to death,

651
00:24:31,550 --> 00:24:34,350
with permanent deprivation
of political rights.

652
00:25:04,400 --> 00:25:05,270
When you were in law school,

653
00:25:05,270 --> 00:25:06,350
didn't your teachers teach you

654
00:25:06,350 --> 00:25:07,440
about nullum crimen sine lege

655
00:25:07,440 --> 00:25:09,500
and proportionality of punishment?

656
00:25:10,750 --> 00:25:12,110
Zhou Yipu was your teacher.

657
00:25:12,110 --> 00:25:13,570
He definitely taught you.

658
00:25:16,510 --> 00:25:17,000
Yes.

659
00:25:18,200 --> 00:25:18,510
Right.

660
00:25:18,510 --> 00:25:19,910
I forgot I am your mentor.

661
00:25:20,790 --> 00:25:22,250
I failed to teach you well.

662
00:25:23,480 --> 00:25:24,400
Is it the prosecutor's duty

663
00:25:24,400 --> 00:25:27,000
to vent public outrage
on behalf of the people?

664
00:25:30,210 --> 00:25:31,000
I remember you said

665
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:32,530
Wang Youxi deserved to die.

666
00:25:33,440 --> 00:25:34,160
Happy now?

667
00:25:35,440 --> 00:25:36,170
He got death.

668
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:37,610
Death penalty.

669
00:25:50,160 --> 00:25:51,560
What are you looking for?

670
00:25:53,510 --> 00:25:54,840
You're not in a hurry now?

671
00:25:54,840 --> 00:25:56,640
Didn't someone in your family
have a sudden illness?

672
00:25:56,640 --> 00:25:57,790
What family?

673
00:25:58,510 --> 00:25:59,570
The piglet is sick.

674
00:26:00,590 --> 00:26:01,850
Are you leaving or not?

675
00:26:02,400 --> 00:26:04,200
I wanted to make ten yuan off you.

676
00:26:05,310 --> 00:26:05,920
Just wait.

677
00:26:12,270 --> 00:26:12,750
Sir.

678
00:26:13,400 --> 00:26:13,980
Did the river

679
00:26:13,980 --> 00:26:15,410
flood two months back?

680
00:26:15,790 --> 00:26:16,070
Yes.

681
00:26:18,310 --> 00:26:19,160
It rose up to

682
00:26:19,480 --> 00:26:20,830
about this high.

683
00:26:21,510 --> 00:26:22,680
The river was

684
00:26:23,310 --> 00:26:24,510
about 60 meters wide.

685
00:26:24,720 --> 00:26:25,310
Now,

686
00:26:26,000 --> 00:26:27,600
it's about 30 meters across.

687
00:26:30,000 --> 00:26:31,260
The place you passed by

688
00:26:31,440 --> 00:26:32,570
is Xiashui Village.

689
00:26:33,110 --> 00:26:33,910
Where you just

690
00:26:34,260 --> 00:26:35,310
waded through the water

691
00:26:35,310 --> 00:26:37,170
is where they pulled out the body.

692
00:26:38,830 --> 00:26:39,720
Didn't they say another part

693
00:26:39,720 --> 00:26:40,970
was found in that grove?

694
00:26:40,970 --> 00:26:41,730
Where is

695
00:26:42,310 --> 00:26:42,970
that grove?

696
00:26:44,960 --> 00:26:45,620
Over there.

697
00:26:46,480 --> 00:26:47,080
See?

698
00:26:47,110 --> 00:26:48,110
Across the river?

699
00:26:48,400 --> 00:26:49,400
How do I get there?

700
00:26:49,520 --> 00:26:50,830
About four or five miles up,

701
00:26:50,830 --> 00:26:52,290
there's a pontoon bridge.

702
00:26:52,310 --> 00:26:53,330
Even on my tractor,

703
00:26:53,330 --> 00:26:54,530
it'd take you a while.

704
00:26:55,200 --> 00:26:55,660
Well...

705
00:26:55,920 --> 00:26:56,850
Just one bridge?

706
00:26:57,080 --> 00:26:58,070
Where the water is shallow,

707
00:26:58,070 --> 00:26:59,200
you can wade across.

708
00:27:00,590 --> 00:27:02,050
What about when it's high?

709
00:27:02,760 --> 00:27:04,760
It depends on your swimming skills.

710
00:27:04,910 --> 00:27:06,640
If you're good, you can swim it.

711
00:27:08,680 --> 00:27:09,070
No.

712
00:27:21,550 --> 00:27:22,750
If you're not leaving,

713
00:27:22,750 --> 00:27:23,750
I'm heading back.

714
00:27:25,270 --> 00:27:25,680
Okay.

715
00:27:28,680 --> 00:27:29,350
Remember,

716
00:27:30,000 --> 00:27:31,680
make sure you take the bridge back.

717
00:27:31,680 --> 00:27:34,240
Don't try swimming
if you're not a strong swimmer.

718
00:27:34,240 --> 00:27:35,510
It's deep in the middle.

719
00:27:35,510 --> 00:27:37,040
Lots of people drown there.

720
00:27:37,160 --> 00:27:37,550
OK.

721
00:28:46,310 --> 00:28:47,000
Waiter!

722
00:28:47,960 --> 00:28:49,620
Give me 100 bottles of yogurt!

723
00:28:50,110 --> 00:28:50,920
100 bottles!

724
00:28:55,720 --> 00:28:57,110
You've tried your best.

725
00:28:57,180 --> 00:28:58,840
Life still goes on.

726
00:29:02,510 --> 00:29:04,770
Qian Xingliang will definitely appeal.

727
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:06,160
The case will go to

728
00:29:06,160 --> 00:29:08,110
the Provincial High Court for appeal.

729
00:29:08,110 --> 00:29:08,700
So?

730
00:29:09,160 --> 00:29:10,690
You're still not taking it?

731
00:29:11,000 --> 00:29:12,330
I really did talk to Mr. Yuan.

732
00:29:12,330 --> 00:29:13,240
He's too busy.

733
00:29:13,640 --> 00:29:14,440
He's too busy.

734
00:29:14,830 --> 00:29:15,690
What about you?

735
00:29:17,440 --> 00:29:18,640
Do you want the truth?

736
00:29:18,880 --> 00:29:19,480
Of course.

737
00:29:23,350 --> 00:29:25,080
This case can't be overturned.

738
00:29:25,160 --> 00:29:25,790
Why?

739
00:29:26,880 --> 00:29:28,830
You went astray from the beginning.

740
00:29:28,830 --> 00:29:30,370
Whether the victim was Yu Sanhua,

741
00:29:30,370 --> 00:29:31,660
or whether the body was even hers,

742
00:29:31,660 --> 00:29:33,990
Qian Xingliang couldn't have killed her.

743
00:29:34,240 --> 00:29:35,350
Why do you say that?

744
00:29:36,070 --> 00:29:37,920
Qian Xingliang didn't have the time.

745
00:29:37,920 --> 00:29:38,550
They couldn't have

746
00:29:38,550 --> 00:29:39,950
missed that, could they?

747
00:29:40,270 --> 00:29:41,330
I'll get you five bottles first.

748
00:29:41,330 --> 00:29:42,200
Let me know if you need more.

749
00:29:42,200 --> 00:29:43,330
Here, I'll help you.

750
00:29:46,560 --> 00:29:47,560
You need evidence

751
00:29:47,590 --> 00:29:48,480
to make such judgment.

752
00:29:48,480 --> 00:29:49,400
Of course.

753
00:29:49,560 --> 00:29:50,590
The first crime scene

754
00:29:50,590 --> 00:29:51,790
the primary crime scene

755
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:52,800
was in the woods

756
00:29:52,830 --> 00:29:54,510
about two miles from Xiashui Village.

757
00:29:54,510 --> 00:29:56,000
The murderer killed there,

758
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:56,670
dismembered the body,

759
00:29:56,670 --> 00:29:58,330
left some parts there,

760
00:29:58,720 --> 00:29:59,850
threw some in the river,

761
00:29:59,850 --> 00:30:00,400
and dumped others

762
00:30:00,400 --> 00:30:01,270
in a cornfield.

763
00:30:01,590 --> 00:30:01,990
Right?

764
00:30:02,590 --> 00:30:04,320
But that's not in the case file.

765
00:30:04,560 --> 00:30:05,790
That's the straight-line distance.

766
00:30:05,790 --> 00:30:08,320
Those woods are on the other side
of the river.

767
00:30:09,110 --> 00:30:10,240
Whether Qian Xingliang

768
00:30:10,240 --> 00:30:11,370
couldn't remember,

769
00:30:11,510 --> 00:30:12,370
was scared,

770
00:30:12,400 --> 00:30:13,680
or colluded with others—

771
00:30:13,680 --> 00:30:15,000
multiple people confirmed

772
00:30:15,000 --> 00:30:17,270
that he was at the village entrance
playing cards

773
00:30:17,270 --> 00:30:18,270
from around six or seven

774
00:30:18,270 --> 00:30:19,800
until after ten each night.

775
00:30:20,360 --> 00:30:21,440
But that still doesn't prove

776
00:30:21,440 --> 00:30:22,680
he didn't have time to commit the crime.

777
00:30:22,680 --> 00:30:24,350
Have you been to the crime scene?

778
00:30:24,350 --> 00:30:25,350
Quit stalling and

779
00:30:25,790 --> 00:30:26,550
keep talking.

780
00:30:26,550 --> 00:30:27,270
Do you know how long

781
00:30:27,270 --> 00:30:28,530
dismemberment takes?

782
00:30:28,560 --> 00:30:30,080
An experienced butcher

783
00:30:30,110 --> 00:30:30,960
takes over ten minutes

784
00:30:30,960 --> 00:30:31,700
to butcher a pig.

785
00:30:31,700 --> 00:30:33,240
Someone without experience?

786
00:30:33,240 --> 00:30:33,770
How long?

787
00:30:34,080 --> 00:30:35,540
I worked on one leg myself,

788
00:30:35,550 --> 00:30:36,810
and it took me forever.

789
00:30:37,510 --> 00:30:38,680
Now think about this:

790
00:30:38,680 --> 00:30:39,590
Yu Sanhua was right there

791
00:30:39,590 --> 00:30:40,750
with Qian Xingliang.

792
00:30:40,750 --> 00:30:42,400
If he wanted to hurry, could she keep up?

793
00:30:42,400 --> 00:30:43,000
Then what?

794
00:30:43,350 --> 00:30:44,250
Race him there?

795
00:30:44,550 --> 00:30:45,590
What if they hitched a ride

796
00:30:45,590 --> 00:30:46,660
on a tractor or farm vehicle?

797
00:30:46,660 --> 00:30:47,160
Then there'd be

798
00:30:47,160 --> 00:30:48,760
witnesses, wouldn't there?

799
00:30:48,790 --> 00:30:50,400
This case made a huge splash.

800
00:30:50,400 --> 00:30:51,000
So how come

801
00:30:51,000 --> 00:30:51,590
they've been looking for so long

802
00:30:51,590 --> 00:30:53,160
and haven't found a single witness?

803
00:30:53,160 --> 00:30:54,360
Let me put it this way:

804
00:30:54,480 --> 00:30:55,830
If Qian Xingliang wanted to kill her,

805
00:30:55,830 --> 00:30:57,560
he would have needed more time.

806
00:30:59,160 --> 00:30:59,880
What?

807
00:31:02,720 --> 00:31:04,880
This localized keratin buildup

808
00:31:04,900 --> 00:31:06,860
on the sole of the foot—

809
00:31:07,070 --> 00:31:08,400
commonly known as a corn.

810
00:31:08,400 --> 00:31:09,270
Qian Xingliang, around that time,

811
00:31:09,270 --> 00:31:10,470
had a corn on his heel.

812
00:31:10,590 --> 00:31:11,480
And it was infected.

813
00:31:11,480 --> 00:31:13,160
Look at mine, this is just a mild case.

814
00:31:13,160 --> 00:31:14,310
But Qian Xingliang's feet?

815
00:31:14,310 --> 00:31:15,750
They were worse than mine.

816
00:31:15,750 --> 00:31:16,680
How fast could he walk?

817
00:31:16,680 --> 00:31:17,740
How far could he go?

818
00:31:18,070 --> 00:31:18,750
Qian Xingliang couldn't have

819
00:31:18,750 --> 00:31:20,750
had enough time to commit the crime.

820
00:31:20,880 --> 00:31:22,110
What time is it now?

821
00:31:23,030 --> 00:31:24,230
My watch has stopped.

822
00:31:24,510 --> 00:31:25,240
Ten o'clock.

823
00:31:25,350 --> 00:31:26,210
Is it accurate?

824
00:31:26,680 --> 00:31:27,000
Yes.

825
00:31:32,680 --> 00:31:34,350
Returning the file won't help.

826
00:31:34,350 --> 00:31:35,110
That's why I said

827
00:31:35,110 --> 00:31:37,110
they're pretending not to see
what's obvious.

828
00:31:37,110 --> 00:31:38,270
Knowing it's impossible,
but doing it anyway;

829
00:31:38,270 --> 00:31:39,200
that's Mr. Yuan,

830
00:31:39,270 --> 00:31:39,960
not me.

831
00:31:40,400 --> 00:31:41,750
But if I'm to know it's impossible,

832
00:31:41,750 --> 00:31:43,640
I must understand why it's impossible.

833
00:31:43,640 --> 00:31:44,720
That's exactly why

834
00:31:44,790 --> 00:31:46,110
I only do non-litigation work.

835
00:31:46,110 --> 00:31:47,710
I don't do criminal defense.

836
00:31:52,160 --> 00:31:53,760
Drink up. They're all yours.

837
00:31:53,960 --> 00:31:55,020
All yours. Come on.

838
00:32:00,160 --> 00:32:01,790
Let me briefly sum up

839
00:32:01,790 --> 00:32:03,030
last week's work.

840
00:32:05,510 --> 00:32:07,370
The cases we prosecuted last week

841
00:32:08,030 --> 00:32:09,160
all yielded satisfactory

842
00:32:09,160 --> 00:32:09,880
outcomes.

843
00:32:10,160 --> 00:32:11,550
Especially, the Wang Youxi

844
00:32:11,550 --> 00:32:13,270
and Liang Yuemin hooliganism case—

845
00:32:13,270 --> 00:32:14,110
one death sentence,

846
00:32:14,110 --> 00:32:15,120
one death with reprieve.

847
00:32:15,120 --> 00:32:15,960
The verdicts had

848
00:32:15,960 --> 00:32:17,690
a very positive social impact.

849
00:32:17,880 --> 00:32:19,310
That very day, members of the public

850
00:32:19,310 --> 00:32:21,680
set off firecrackers
outside the courthouse

851
00:32:21,680 --> 00:32:22,590
and presented the court with a banner

852
00:32:22,590 --> 00:32:24,220
reading "Ridding the People of Scourges."

853
00:32:24,220 --> 00:32:26,220
The banner went to the court,

854
00:32:26,400 --> 00:32:28,480
but we in the Procuratorate
share in the credit.

855
00:32:28,480 --> 00:32:29,810
It is truly gratifying.

856
00:32:30,090 --> 00:32:30,610
Here,

857
00:32:30,640 --> 00:32:31,680
I'd especially like to commend

858
00:32:31,680 --> 00:32:32,940
comrade Chen Yizhong.

859
00:32:33,310 --> 00:32:34,030
This was his

860
00:32:34,160 --> 00:32:36,550
very first case as lead prosecutor,

861
00:32:36,830 --> 00:32:38,830
and he achieved such a great result.

862
00:32:38,920 --> 00:32:39,980
Congratulations.

863
00:32:49,790 --> 00:32:51,550
And the Qian Xingliang murder case

864
00:32:51,550 --> 00:32:52,610
was also a success.

865
00:32:54,920 --> 00:32:55,980
Chief Prosecutor.

866
00:32:59,200 --> 00:33:00,030
I think...

867
00:33:02,400 --> 00:33:03,340
I think Wang Youxi's case

868
00:33:03,340 --> 00:33:04,540
was over-sentenced.

869
00:33:05,440 --> 00:33:07,040
Can we file a protest appeal?

870
00:33:10,440 --> 00:33:11,240
What's wrong?

871
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:12,720
Didn't you request

872
00:33:12,720 --> 00:33:15,050
a sentence beyond the statutory penalty?

873
00:33:15,240 --> 00:33:15,680
Yes.

874
00:33:17,960 --> 00:33:18,760
I admit it.

875
00:33:19,240 --> 00:33:20,790
At the time, I was truly

876
00:33:20,790 --> 00:33:21,640
overwhelmed by the heinousness

877
00:33:21,640 --> 00:33:22,570
of their crimes.

878
00:33:23,790 --> 00:33:25,980
I forgot the principle of proportionality.

879
00:33:25,980 --> 00:33:26,880
When I recommended

880
00:33:26,880 --> 00:33:27,830
sentencing above the statutory range,

881
00:33:27,830 --> 00:33:28,680
what I had in mind

882
00:33:28,680 --> 00:33:29,480
was ten years,

883
00:33:29,510 --> 00:33:31,110
thirteen at the absolute most.

884
00:33:31,110 --> 00:33:32,110
That's why I didn't

885
00:33:32,110 --> 00:33:35,170
give the court a specific
sentencing recommendation.

886
00:33:35,310 --> 00:33:36,000
But I didn't expect

887
00:33:36,000 --> 00:33:37,800
they'd get two death sentences.

888
00:33:38,510 --> 00:33:39,570
Chief Prosecutor.

889
00:33:39,720 --> 00:33:41,270
They truly don't deserve to die.

890
00:33:41,270 --> 00:33:42,930
If we punish beyond the crime,

891
00:33:43,400 --> 00:33:44,070
we lose the solemnity

892
00:33:44,070 --> 00:33:44,920
of the law.

893
00:33:45,030 --> 00:33:47,070
It was we who demanded harsh punishment.

894
00:33:47,070 --> 00:33:48,200
Once the verdict came out,

895
00:33:48,200 --> 00:33:49,550
public opinion was supportive.

896
00:33:49,550 --> 00:33:51,160
If we file a protest appeal now,

897
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:53,290
aren't we just slapping our own faces?

898
00:33:53,440 --> 00:33:54,120
I understand.

899
00:33:54,120 --> 00:33:55,400
I get it, Chief Prosecutor.

900
00:33:55,400 --> 00:33:56,310
But the maximum sentence

901
00:33:56,310 --> 00:33:58,370
for hooliganism is only seven years.

902
00:33:58,880 --> 00:33:59,510
No matter how much we increase it,

903
00:33:59,510 --> 00:34:01,710
it shouldn't go up to the death penalty.

904
00:34:03,640 --> 00:34:05,240
If we let this verdict stand,

905
00:34:06,400 --> 00:34:07,440
we won't be able to handle

906
00:34:07,440 --> 00:34:09,100
future cases of hooliganism.

907
00:34:11,110 --> 00:34:11,510
Lin,

908
00:34:12,880 --> 00:34:13,880
what do you think?

909
00:34:16,710 --> 00:34:17,570
Prosecutor Xu.

910
00:34:18,550 --> 00:34:19,190
I agree.

911
00:34:19,850 --> 00:34:20,630
If their crime

912
00:34:20,630 --> 00:34:21,889
only gets seven years,

913
00:34:22,510 --> 00:34:23,760
the public may not accept it.

914
00:34:23,760 --> 00:34:25,420
But if it's the death penalty,

915
00:34:25,510 --> 00:34:26,630
the law loses its

916
00:34:26,630 --> 00:34:28,090
benchmark significance.

917
00:34:28,110 --> 00:34:29,670
Just as Chen said,

918
00:34:30,070 --> 00:34:32,600
how will we handle
future hooliganism cases?

919
00:34:32,889 --> 00:34:33,760
Didn't you two reach

920
00:34:33,760 --> 00:34:35,159
a consensus beforehand?

921
00:34:35,190 --> 00:34:36,230
It's on me. My fault.

922
00:34:36,230 --> 00:34:37,830
I failed in my duty to remind.

923
00:34:37,889 --> 00:34:39,070
Mr. Lin did remind me.

924
00:34:39,070 --> 00:34:39,630
But at that time,

925
00:34:39,630 --> 00:34:40,960
I just wouldn't listen.

926
00:34:41,960 --> 00:34:42,920
Chief Prosecutor.

927
00:34:42,920 --> 00:34:43,940
The office can discipline me,

928
00:34:43,940 --> 00:34:45,199
but we absolutely

929
00:34:45,230 --> 00:34:46,360
must file a protest.

930
00:34:46,670 --> 00:34:47,670
We made a mistake,

931
00:34:47,880 --> 00:34:49,030
and we still have the chance
to correct it.

932
00:34:49,030 --> 00:34:49,550
But the criminals

933
00:34:49,550 --> 00:34:51,280
also need the chance to repent.

934
00:34:52,030 --> 00:34:52,960
If they are dead,

935
00:34:52,960 --> 00:34:53,489
then I...

936
00:34:54,510 --> 00:34:56,110
then none of us have a chance.

937
00:35:08,800 --> 00:35:10,260
What does everyone think?

938
00:35:12,440 --> 00:35:13,070
I agree.

939
00:35:14,110 --> 00:35:15,880
Death penalty is indeed too harsh.

940
00:35:15,880 --> 00:35:16,480
But

941
00:35:16,760 --> 00:35:18,490
how can we face public opinion?

942
00:35:19,030 --> 00:35:20,280
Didn't you think about that

943
00:35:20,280 --> 00:35:22,010
when you filed the indictment?

944
00:35:23,630 --> 00:35:24,030
Fine.

945
00:35:25,630 --> 00:35:27,360
I'll bring it to the
Procuratorial Committee.

946
00:35:27,360 --> 00:35:28,420
Whether to protest

947
00:35:29,480 --> 00:35:31,210
is for the Committee to decide.

948
00:35:35,880 --> 00:35:38,080
Binjiang Intermediate People's Court

949
00:35:38,320 --> 00:35:39,480
hereby publicly tries

950
00:35:39,480 --> 00:35:41,630
the case of the Yao Bo hooligan gang,

951
00:35:42,440 --> 00:35:43,630
prosecuted by

952
00:35:44,110 --> 00:35:46,070
the Binjiang City People's Procuratorate.

953
00:35:46,070 --> 00:35:47,270
Court is reconvened.

954
00:35:47,480 --> 00:35:48,880
Bring in the defendants.

955
00:36:04,440 --> 00:36:05,440
Presiding Judge.

956
00:36:06,510 --> 00:36:07,630
The plaintiff's side

957
00:36:07,630 --> 00:36:09,590
requests to question the defendant

958
00:36:09,590 --> 00:36:12,280
regarding key facts of this case.

959
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:13,930
You may proceed.

960
00:36:15,590 --> 00:36:16,250
Defendant.

961
00:36:17,560 --> 00:36:18,850
I, as defense counsel,

962
00:36:18,880 --> 00:36:20,590
will now question you

963
00:36:20,590 --> 00:36:22,320
regarding the criminal facts.

964
00:36:23,960 --> 00:36:25,960
The indictment explicitly charges

965
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:27,400
that you used nude photos

966
00:36:27,670 --> 00:36:29,800
to control the victim, Qiao Yuanyuan,

967
00:36:30,200 --> 00:36:31,120
and forced her

968
00:36:31,720 --> 00:36:33,370
to have sexual relations

969
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:34,800
with other gang members.

970
00:36:35,510 --> 00:36:37,310
You also made her pay 20,000 yuan

971
00:36:37,360 --> 00:36:38,820
to buy back the negatives.

972
00:36:39,030 --> 00:36:40,760
Is this true?

973
00:36:41,320 --> 00:36:42,800
Do you have any objection?

974
00:36:44,360 --> 00:36:45,260
Those nude photos

975
00:36:45,260 --> 00:36:46,660
were taken by Xiaoguang.

976
00:36:47,550 --> 00:36:48,110
When he got bored,

977
00:36:48,110 --> 00:36:49,770
he passed Qiao Yuanyuan to me.

978
00:36:50,510 --> 00:36:51,800
And the 20,000 yuan was also

979
00:36:51,800 --> 00:36:53,130
demanded by Xiaoguang.

980
00:36:54,590 --> 00:36:56,590
I just don't understand how she could

981
00:36:56,590 --> 00:36:58,510
jump into the river
over something like that.

982
00:36:58,510 --> 00:36:59,570
Are you even human?

983
00:37:00,550 --> 00:37:01,080
Bastard!

984
00:37:01,230 --> 00:37:01,630
You should

985
00:37:01,630 --> 00:37:03,110
all be shot!

986
00:37:03,130 --> 00:37:04,090
Order, please!

987
00:37:05,150 --> 00:37:06,880
If you disrupt the court again,

988
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:09,050
you'll be removed from the courtroom!

989
00:37:10,510 --> 00:37:11,510
Presiding Judge.

990
00:37:12,670 --> 00:37:13,800
We didn't see

991
00:37:14,760 --> 00:37:15,760
anyone named Song Xiaoguang

992
00:37:15,760 --> 00:37:16,960
in the indictment.

993
00:37:17,550 --> 00:37:18,170
However,

994
00:37:18,360 --> 00:37:20,220
during these court proceedings,

995
00:37:20,440 --> 00:37:21,710
more than one defendant

996
00:37:21,710 --> 00:37:23,110
mentioned Song Xiaoguang,

997
00:37:23,110 --> 00:37:24,510
stating that many things

998
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:26,120
were directed by him.

999
00:37:26,510 --> 00:37:27,800
And this gang

1000
00:37:28,360 --> 00:37:29,490
was gathered by him.

1001
00:37:30,590 --> 00:37:31,710
So we'd like to ask:

1002
00:37:33,030 --> 00:37:34,590
where is Song Xiaoguang?

1003
00:37:36,080 --> 00:37:37,520
Why is he not on

1004
00:37:37,550 --> 00:37:38,880
the list of defendants?

1005
00:37:42,960 --> 00:37:43,510
Counsel.

1006
00:37:44,550 --> 00:37:45,760
You are representing

1007
00:37:46,280 --> 00:37:48,030
the civil compensation portion.

1008
00:37:48,030 --> 00:37:49,690
You may direct your questions

1009
00:37:49,710 --> 00:37:50,840
to that aspect only.

1010
00:37:51,490 --> 00:37:52,320
But that's exactly

1011
00:37:52,320 --> 00:37:53,630
what we're doing.

1012
00:37:54,480 --> 00:37:55,920
And as you just heard,

1013
00:37:56,400 --> 00:37:58,000
the 20,000 yuan was demanded

1014
00:37:58,110 --> 00:37:59,190
by Song Xiaoguang.

1015
00:37:59,710 --> 00:38:00,640
If he's not here,

1016
00:38:01,240 --> 00:38:02,000
we can't exercise

1017
00:38:02,000 --> 00:38:03,000
our rights.

1018
00:38:05,920 --> 00:38:06,960
Your question

1019
00:38:07,510 --> 00:38:09,310
has been recorded by this court.

1020
00:38:09,480 --> 00:38:10,110
Proceed.

1021
00:38:19,510 --> 00:38:20,170
Defendant,

1022
00:38:20,890 --> 00:38:22,000
the indictment charges you

1023
00:38:22,000 --> 00:38:23,230
over the course of more than a year,

1024
00:38:23,230 --> 00:38:25,360
you repeatedly vandalized
the Yunshang Nightclub,

1025
00:38:25,360 --> 00:38:26,360
causing my client

1026
00:38:26,480 --> 00:38:27,280
direct economic losses

1027
00:38:27,280 --> 00:38:28,510
of over 100,000 yuan.

1028
00:38:29,110 --> 00:38:29,630
To this,

1029
00:38:30,150 --> 00:38:31,410
what do you want to say?

1030
00:38:31,450 --> 00:38:32,510
Song Xiaoguang led it.

1031
00:38:32,510 --> 00:38:33,640
I didn't dare not go.

1032
00:38:34,210 --> 00:38:35,190
If I didn't go,

1033
00:38:36,090 --> 00:38:37,950
he'd enforce his own discipline.

1034
00:38:38,360 --> 00:38:39,090
Discipline?

1035
00:38:39,920 --> 00:38:40,920
What discipline?

1036
00:38:41,150 --> 00:38:42,550
A beating, if it's light.

1037
00:38:43,110 --> 00:38:44,280
If it's heavy, you end up crippled.

1038
00:38:44,280 --> 00:38:44,840
Look.

1039
00:38:46,360 --> 00:38:47,690
This is his discipline.

1040
00:38:53,510 --> 00:38:54,400
Presiding Judge.

1041
00:38:54,400 --> 00:38:55,510
According to the defendant,

1042
00:38:55,510 --> 00:38:56,360
the one who caused my client

1043
00:38:56,360 --> 00:38:57,590
economic losses

1044
00:38:57,610 --> 00:38:59,340
was primarily Song Xiaoguang.

1045
00:39:00,140 --> 00:39:01,400
So we have to ask again:

1046
00:39:01,880 --> 00:39:03,280
where is Song Xiaoguang?

1047
00:39:05,440 --> 00:39:06,860
As the organizer of this gang

1048
00:39:06,860 --> 00:39:07,860
and the one giving orders,

1049
00:39:07,860 --> 00:39:08,740
why is he not

1050
00:39:08,770 --> 00:39:10,430
appearing in this courtroom?

1051
00:39:19,920 --> 00:39:21,320
Please answer our query.

1052
00:39:27,510 --> 00:39:28,590
We only try

1053
00:39:29,030 --> 00:39:29,920
what is in

1054
00:39:30,360 --> 00:39:31,290
the indictment.

1055
00:39:31,590 --> 00:39:32,250
Objection.

1056
00:39:33,110 --> 00:39:34,630
Trying a gang case

1057
00:39:35,480 --> 00:39:37,280
while the gang leader is absent,

1058
00:39:38,150 --> 00:39:39,610
what kind of trial is this?

1059
00:39:40,930 --> 00:39:41,850
Does the law

1060
00:39:41,880 --> 00:39:43,340
only apply to some people,

1061
00:39:44,230 --> 00:39:45,430
while leaving others

1062
00:39:45,670 --> 00:39:46,760
helpless?

1063
00:39:48,110 --> 00:39:49,170
How can such a trial

1064
00:39:49,630 --> 00:39:50,760
convince the public

1065
00:39:50,800 --> 00:39:52,260
or demonstrate fairness?

1066
00:39:53,110 --> 00:39:54,370
So we strongly request

1067
00:39:54,760 --> 00:39:55,890
that Song Xiaoguang

1068
00:39:55,960 --> 00:39:56,920
must be brought to court

1069
00:39:56,920 --> 00:39:57,780
to stand trial.

1070
00:39:58,920 --> 00:40:00,550
The investigative authorities have

1071
00:40:00,550 --> 00:40:01,940
conducted a forensic psychiatric

1072
00:40:01,940 --> 00:40:03,820
evaluation of Song Xiaoguang

1073
00:40:04,480 --> 00:40:06,070
and confirmed that he suffers

1074
00:40:06,070 --> 00:40:07,270
from schizophrenia.

1075
00:40:07,670 --> 00:40:08,660
He is currently

1076
00:40:08,920 --> 00:40:10,480
a person without criminal responsibility

1077
00:40:10,480 --> 00:40:12,360
and has been sent
to a psychiatric hospital

1078
00:40:12,360 --> 00:40:13,220
for treatment.

1079
00:40:13,920 --> 00:40:14,880
We have reason

1080
00:40:15,230 --> 00:40:17,640
to doubt the authenticity
of this evaluation

1081
00:40:17,640 --> 00:40:19,720
and request a different institution

1082
00:40:21,070 --> 00:40:22,600
to conduct a new evaluation

1083
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,280
of Song Xiaoguang's mental state,

1084
00:40:24,280 --> 00:40:25,550
to distinguish truth from falsehood,

1085
00:40:25,550 --> 00:40:27,750
and to restore the integrity of the law.

1086
00:40:30,710 --> 00:40:31,880
Bring Song Xiaoguang!

1087
00:40:31,880 --> 00:40:33,630
All are equal before the law!

1088
00:40:34,840 --> 00:40:36,100
Bring Song Xiaoguang!

1089
00:40:36,280 --> 00:40:38,400
All are equal before the law!

1090
00:40:41,510 --> 00:40:43,110
All are equal before the law!

1091
00:40:43,550 --> 00:40:45,800
Bring Song Xiaoguang!

1092
00:40:45,840 --> 00:40:47,240
Where is Song Xiaoguang?

1093
00:40:47,800 --> 00:40:48,440
Order!

1094
00:40:48,590 --> 00:40:49,550
Bring Song Xiaoguang!

1095
00:40:49,550 --> 00:40:50,480
Order!

1096
00:40:51,510 --> 00:40:52,150
Order!

1097
00:40:53,710 --> 00:40:54,320
The court

1098
00:40:56,030 --> 00:40:56,830
is adjourned.

1099
00:41:14,950 --> 00:41:15,800
Coming.

1100
00:41:22,960 --> 00:41:24,190
Who are you looking for?

1101
00:41:24,190 --> 00:41:25,320
I'm looking for you.

1102
00:41:25,320 --> 00:41:26,250
Who are you?

1103
00:41:26,670 --> 00:41:27,670
I'm Xia Yingjie.

1104
00:41:28,110 --> 00:41:29,640
I'm Lu Zeming's classmate.

1105
00:41:30,440 --> 00:41:31,840
During the Li Xiang case,

1106
00:41:31,920 --> 00:41:32,800
we met.

1107
00:41:34,750 --> 00:41:35,550
The Li Xiang case.

1108
00:41:35,550 --> 00:41:37,410
I first saw you at the university,

1109
00:41:37,510 --> 00:41:39,640
and then we all went to Nanyu together.

1110
00:41:47,710 --> 00:41:49,040
So what brings you to me?

1111
00:41:49,550 --> 00:41:50,150
It's late.

1112
00:41:50,880 --> 00:41:52,550
Can we talk about it tomorrow?

1113
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:53,800
I know you are

1114
00:41:53,800 --> 00:41:54,800
returning to Beijing tomorrow.

1115
00:41:54,800 --> 00:41:56,110
I was afraid it'd be too late.

1116
00:41:56,110 --> 00:41:56,630
Can I ask

1117
00:41:56,630 --> 00:41:57,960
what you do for a living?

1118
00:41:59,550 --> 00:42:00,150
I am

1119
00:42:01,690 --> 00:42:03,280
a judge at the Binjiang Intermediate

1120
00:42:03,280 --> 00:42:04,210
People's Court.

1121
00:42:04,590 --> 00:42:05,920
I'm also the associate judge

1122
00:42:05,920 --> 00:42:07,110
on the Qian Xingliang case.

1123
00:42:07,110 --> 00:42:08,070
I came to see you because

1124
00:42:08,070 --> 00:42:10,200
I wanted to talk to you about that case.

1125
00:42:13,070 --> 00:42:13,800
Comrade Xia.

1126
00:42:15,520 --> 00:42:16,960
Given your current position,

1127
00:42:16,960 --> 00:42:18,550
coming to see me at this hour

1128
00:42:19,150 --> 00:42:19,920
to talk about

1129
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:21,480
a case I know nothing about.

1130
00:42:21,510 --> 00:42:22,800
It's not appropriate.

1131
00:42:24,550 --> 00:42:26,150
I know it's not appropriate.

1132
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:28,100
And I know it's presumptuous.

1133
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:31,320
Or maybe

1134
00:42:31,550 --> 00:42:32,670
we could have Lu Zeming

1135
00:42:32,670 --> 00:42:33,130
join us?

1136
00:42:33,150 --> 00:42:33,670
I don't want

1137
00:42:33,670 --> 00:42:34,800
a third person here.

1138
00:42:36,760 --> 00:42:38,000
Then let me grab my coat.

1139
00:42:38,000 --> 00:42:38,800
Let's talk in the lobby.

1140
00:42:38,800 --> 00:42:39,730
Sorry, Mr. Yuan,

1141
00:42:39,850 --> 00:42:41,120
but I'd also prefer

1142
00:42:41,150 --> 00:42:42,800
not to be seen talking to you.

1143
00:42:43,630 --> 00:42:44,230
After all,

1144
00:42:45,150 --> 00:42:46,610
Binjiang is a small place.

1145
00:42:48,190 --> 00:42:49,440
Yes, it is.

1146
00:42:51,110 --> 00:42:52,150
Binjiang is small.

1147
00:42:52,150 --> 00:42:52,710
Mr. Yuan.

1148
00:42:53,290 --> 00:42:54,220
I'll only take up

1149
00:42:54,230 --> 00:42:55,630
ten minutes of your time.

1150
00:42:56,760 --> 00:42:57,510
But these might be

1151
00:42:57,510 --> 00:42:58,880
the last ten minutes

1152
00:42:58,880 --> 00:42:59,840
we have to save an innocent life.
